  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="38.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 38.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ á swa man byð mihtigra oððe maran hádes, swa scæl he deoppor for Gode ⁊ for worulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-a">And á swa man byð mihtra oððe maran hades, swa sceal he deoppor for Gode ⁊ for weorulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-q">Semperque, sicut homo potentior est uel maioris ordinis, sic debet sollertius pro Deo et seculo quod iniustum est emendare.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="38.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ a swa man bið mihtigra oððe maran hades, swa sceal hé deoppor for Gode ⁊ for worulde unriht gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And in all cases, the greater a man is and the higher his rank, the more stringent shall be the amends which he shall be required to make to God and to men for lawless behaviour.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und je mächtiger oder höheren Standes immer jemand ist, um so tiefer soll er Unrecht kirchlich und weltlich büssen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And the more powerful or the higher in rank anyone is, the more deeply must he atone for wrong before God and before the world.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 52.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
